Task 1 & 2: Infrastructure Setup
Deploy the VM instance with a static external IP and appropriate firewall rules in the us-east4 region.

Bash
# Delete existing IP and recreate VM
gcloud compute addresses delete xss-test-ip-address --region=us-east4 --quiet
gcloud compute firewall-rules delete enable-wss-scan --quiet

# Recreate static IP
gcloud compute addresses create xss-test-ip-address --region=us-east4

# Create VM Instance
gcloud compute instances create xss-test-vm-instance \
  --address=xss-test-ip-address --no-service-account \
  --no-scopes --machine-type=e2-micro --zone=us-east4-b \
  --metadata=startup-script='apt-get update; apt-get install -y python3-flask'

# Create Firewall Rule for port 8080
gcloud compute firewall-rules create enable-wss-scan \
  --direction=INGRESS --priority=1000 \
  --network=default --action=ALLOW \
  --rules=tcp:8080 --source-ranges=0.0.0.0/0
Task 3 & 4: Enable API and Deploy Application
Enable the Web Security Scanner API and deploy the vulnerable code to the VM.

Bash
# Enable API
gcloud services enable websecurityscanner.googleapis.com

# Deploy vulnerable code via SSH
gcloud compute ssh xss-test-vm-instance --zone=us-east4-b --quiet <<EOF
gsutil cp gs://cloud-training/GCPSEC-ScannerAppEngine/flask_code.tar . && tar xvf flask_code.tar
nohup python3 app.py > app.log 2>&1 &
EOF
Task 5: Vulnerability Remediation
Apply a patch to app.py using sed to enable HTML escaping, then restart the application to verify the fix.

Bash
# Connect to VM and patch the code
gcloud compute ssh xss-test-vm-instance --zone=us-east4-b

# Inside SSH session:
pkill -f "python3 app.py" || true
sed -i 's/#  output_string = "".join/  output_string = "".join/' app.py
sed -i 's/  output_string = input_string/  # output_string = input_string/' app.py
grep "output_string" app.py
nohup python3 app.py > app.log 2>&1 &
exit

# Final restart for verification
gcloud compute ssh xss-test-vm-instance --zone=us-east4-b --command="python3 app.py"
